                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              is given by the composite of two extramural isomorphisms that identify the given homology group with a donor or receptor group, respectively, with a long zigzag of extramural isomorphisms.
          %h3#FourLemma The four lemma
          %p
            We prove the
            %em
              strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/four+lemma"} four lemma
            from the salamander lemma.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              Consider a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
